node_modules/
.rsbuild/
*.log
coverage/

# `dist/` is rsbuild's output -- the SERVER arm's built front end.
dist/

# `payload/` is what `build_payload.py` writes -- the CLIENT arm's pyshim zip,
# the flab2bp wheel and their manifest. It is deliberately NOT `dist/`: rsbuild
# cleans its own output directory on every production build, so while the two
# arms shared `dist/` a single `bun run build` -- which `flab2bp-web` runs by
# itself on first start -- silently deleted the client arm's payload and left
# `worker.js` fetching a 404.
payload/

# NOTE: `public/` was ignored in the standalone dsp-blueprint-viewer repo,
# because there it is regenerated from a local Dyson Sphere Program install by
# `bun run extract-assets`. It is COMMITTED here: without the catalog JSON and
# the icon atlas the viewer renders nothing, and requiring a game install to
# run the web UI of a repo that already vendors FactorioLab's dataset would be
# a strange asymmetry. It is 1.6MB.
